    "conclusion":  "The orthogonal M180 elbow clips the blocked west M-06 search-window overlay. A diagonal transition from (11.25,13.75) through (10.4167,14.25) to (9.6667,15.0) clears assigned static rectangles using an 18 in radius route buffer, while retaining only 0.6 in at the assumed stool proxy, 2 in at the table edge and 0.38 in at the blocked west M-06 search-window boundary. These margins are fragile and do not validate operation; this is a proposal, not a settled approach or layout.",
    "limitations":  [
                        "Room, furniture and search-window geometry are schematic coordinate proxies; route buffer assumes a 36 in-wide path with rounded ends at its centerline.",
                        "Sub-inch stool/window margins and 2 in table margin do not account for movement, tolerances or uncertainty and are insufficient to validate operation.",
                        "The 36 in swept-path model does not establish code compliance or accessibility.",
                        "Physical walls, door leaf/swing/clear width, thresholds, porch connection, services and Revit/IFC are unmodeled.",
